        <p>NOTlCE.—Solvers who become entitled to a prize In this comp3tition can, if they desire, have any book on the game of Draughts equal to the value • -„ -s• Instead of cash prize, by notifying the mraughts Editor.</p>
        <p>In connection with the above competition we vuer a monthly prize of 5s to the competitor who elleceeds in placing himself at the head of the Sol..vers' List at Vie end of the month. Where the prizse is awarded the winn i ers' score s cancelled, th while the rernainiiig clmpetitors' points go towards enter the e next months competition. The winner may re- tourney if he chooses, commencing again at the bottom of the list. Points are awarded as ile°nall"" 1 , Two for the correct solution of a prob- for 11 'w.° for correcting the author's terms, one andB on o iwin forg a dual solution or a dual key-move, One Stage n the 'hewing a dwil continuation at any 6olution.</p>
        <p>--- The diagram we give below will be found to be a Change from the ordinary style of problems. Die object is to levers° the pieces, that iF, the three Black men on 8, 11, 0.,,1 1,5 r:-...ca" be placed on Squares 22, 25,and 29,awi vwe versa with the Whites. Black or White can make any number of moves in succession, hut the men must only be moved one Square at a time,except when jumping over a piece; 'When this occurs, the piecs which is jumped over MlUst not be p4moved from the board, and a piece is net obliged to jump over two in succession as in ordinary draughts. We shill give the solution to this next week.</p>
