        <p>t. Mary's Church, Latchford.—Annual Ball The annual ball in connection with St. Mary's Churcb,lLatchford, took place on Monday even- ' ig in the Parr Hall, and was attended with success xeellent arrangements had been made for the. i'vent by a committee consisting of Messrs. Peter bate, John Barnwell, John Burke, George Dolan, teter Delaney, John Fraser, John Knight, Thomas 44110 y, Robert Lowe, Samuel Ross, John Rabbitt, ti°sePil Smith and G. T. Bibby, credit being due to a last-named gentleman for the manner in which .48 Performed tl:e secretarial duties. About 350 were Zesent, and dancinz commenced at 8 o'clock to e.l45iC supplied by Mr. P. Randall's Band. Messrs „ Wells and T. Curran officiated as M.C.'s. The inelreshments were in the hands of the Ladies' Com- b„it.t!ei and the Hall was decorated with plants lent " .bae Parr Hall Committee. The proceedings ;red off without a hitch, dancing being kept up Spirit till an early hour next morning.</p>
