      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-03-02_WidnesExaminer_art0106" n="art0106">
        <head>YOUR THROAT.</head>
        <p>YOUR THROAT.</p>
        <p>It has been tender lately and rather delicate—you can't uso your voice freely, and your glands seem to throb when you hurry. You've evidently got what is called a relaxes throat and are consequently very liable to catch cold or something more serious. Don't on any consideration trifle with your throat—you don't want to lose your vein° and you must not imperil in any way your breathing apparatus, so get a bottle at once of Levens Lung Linetus—the safest and surest remedy yet produced for all pulmonary affections. Levens Linctus is nice to take, and it does its work quickly and well. One dose you will find brings you relief. A few doses will effect a cure. Lavans Linctus is sold by all Chemists and Co-operative Stores, and post free is 24 9d., 4s 6d. from the Proprietors, Green and Co., Deansgate, Bolton. A man who used to suffer from bronchitis says :—" I had been troubled with bronchitis for over 16 years, and had given up all hope of ever receiving relief—but acting on the advice of a friend; I bought a bottle of Livens Lung Linctus, which at once gave me relief. I then obtained another bottle and now I feel like ' a king,' ,in comparison with what I used to oe. I cannot too highly recommend it to sufferers from bronchitis and similar complaints."</p>
